            "outcome": "VERIFIED",
            "at": "2026-11-02T09:02:43Z"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How-to and procedures",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Use explain to distinguish index access from order provision: IXSCAN identifies index access, while an explicit SORT indicates additional sorting. Merely seeing an index scan is insufficient evidence that the index supplies the requested order. (medium confidence) Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/explain-results.md ; https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/analyze-query-plan.md",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/explain-results.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:510f6cbe28f6f4d136cfde1d2473a6775b4e34e4f45c33e6b725c2eaddf92745",
          "validationStatus": "NOT-SAMPLED",
          "evidenceIds": [],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/OneUptime/blog/blob/master/posts/2026-01-30-mongodb-compound-index-strategies/README.md",
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/tutorial/analyze-query-plan.md"
          ],
          "remediation": {
